sukut (0.4.0~beta.7-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Outputs, as Windows 0.4.2: a newly connected Bluetooth or USB output
    (not HDMI) is used at once, with a notification, and Off gives it the
    default; when it disconnects, Sukut goes back to the previous choice.
  * A chosen output that is missing at Start (headphones off, EasyEffects not
    running yet) no longer fails: Sukut plays on the default and moves to it
    when it appears.
  * An output chosen in the sound settings while Sukut was off is used at the
    next Start; an output chosen in Sukut is kept.
  * Picking, in the sound settings, the output Sukut already plays on no
    longer lets apps bypass Sukut.
  * EasyEffects: a feedback loop (EasyEffects following the default output
    while Sukut plays into it) is stopped at once; apps pinned to Easy Effects
    Sink go through Sukut and get their pins back on Off. The window explains
    each problem and shows the steps ("Using EasyEffects", "How to fix").

 -- الطرفية <altarafiyah@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 20:17:07 +0800

sukut (0.4.0~beta.6-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Tray: the Off icon follows the panel's text colour (white on a dark
    panel, dark on a light one) through KDE's colour-scheme stylesheet, and
    GNOME recolours it as a symbolic icon. Renamed to tray-idle-symbolic so
    no icon cache can show the old dark picture. The Standby menu icon
    adapts the same way.
  * Lower memory: the phone setup pictures are decoded only while open and
    at the size shown (0.8 MB instead of 13 MB each); opening the Phone
    pages peaks at 78 MB instead of 106 MB. The unused wireless-debugging
    picture is no longer installed.

